From: Rex Zhu <Rex.Zhu@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 5 Jun 2018 09:46:46 +0800
Subject: PCI: Add check code for last image indicator not set
Git-commit: beced88e6af43c9653cee09f5111ae7495824e07
Patch-mainline: v4.19-rc1
References: CVE-2026-72487 bsc#1276767

If the "last image" indicator was not set in the PCI data struct, print "No
more image in the PCI ROM" instead of looping back and printing "Invalid
PCI ROM header signature".

Signed-off-by: Rex Zhu <Rex.Zhu@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Helgaas <bhelgaas@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>
Acked-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/pci/rom.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/pci/rom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/rom.c
@@ -109,6 +109,12 @@ size_t pci_get_rom_size(struct pci_dev *
 		/* Avoid iterating through memory outside the resource window */
 		if (image >= rom + size)
 			break;
+		if (!last_image) {
+			if (readw(image) != 0xAA55) {
+				pci_info(pdev, "No more image in the PCI ROM\n");
+				break;
+			}
+		}
 	} while (length && !last_image);
 
 	/* never return a size larger than the PCI resource window */
